## How this bundle was built

This bundle was produced by `wikiforge` from a curator workspace. The curator workspace contains raw sources, draft pages, ingest queues, request inboxes, and an Obsidian vault config — none of which travel into this bundle. What ships here is the frozen, citation-bearing, agent-readable subset.

The build process:

1. Lints the wiki in strict mode; fails on any error.
2. Walks all pages, parses frontmatter, drops `draft: true` and (by default) `confidence: placeholder` pages.
3. Builds `wiki/.meta/pages.tsv` (one row per page) and `wiki/.meta/links.tsv` (one row per edge — `references` for prose links, plus the four typed edges from frontmatter).
4. For each `code-patterns/` page, extracts the cited line range from the pinned repo in the curator's `raw/repos/` tree, prepends a provenance header, writes to `wiki/snippets/<basename>.txt`.
5. Copies `wiki/` and `bin/` into the bundle, renders this `MANIFEST.md` and `SKILL.md`, stamps `VERSION`.

The bundle is read-only by contract. Consumer agents call `bin/wiki-*` and append to `feedback.md`; they never modify wiki pages.
